    "prompt_chars": 3454,
    "reply": "```python\nimport math\n\nSAFE_Z = 0.22          # pad travel height: a held 40 mm cube clears the 60 mm bin walls with wide margin\nCUBE = 0.040\nMAX_CALLS = 280        # stay below the 300-call limit (4 were already spent on perception)\n\n\ndef run(api):\n    calls = [4]\n\n    def budget(n=1):\n        return calls[0] + n <= MAX_CALLS\n\n    def move(x, y, z, yaw):\n        calls[0] += 1\n        api.move_to((x, y, z), yaw)\n\n    def suction(on):\n        calls[0] += 1\n        return api.suction(on)\n\n    def descend(x, y, z_from, z_to, yaw, step=0.03):\n        # Small steps keep the joint-space motion close to a vertical line.\n        z = z_from\n        while z - z_to > step:\n            z -= step\n            move(x, y, z, yaw)\n        move(x, y, z_to, yaw)\n\n    def ascend(x, y, z_from, yaw, step=0.04):\n        z = z_from\n        while SAFE_Z - z > step:\n            z += step\n            move(x, y, z, yaw)\n        move(x, y, SAFE_Z, yaw)\n\n    for attempt in range(4):\n        if not budget(60):\n            break\n\n        # Re-perceive every attempt: trust the camera, not the nominal placement.\n        calls[0] += 1\n        (cx, cy, ctop), cyaw, colour = api.cube_pose()\n        calls[0] += 1\n        (bx, by, brim), byaw = api.bin_pose(colour)\n\n        # --- pick ---\n        move(cx, cy, SAFE_Z, cyaw)\n        descend(cx, cy, SAFE_Z, ctop + 0.010, cyaw)\n        held = False\n        z = ctop + 0.001\n        for i in range(6):                      # creep down 1 mm at a time until the pad grips\n            move(cx, cy, z, cyaw)\n            if suction(True):\n                held = True\n                break\n            z -= 0.001\n        if not held:\n            suction(False)\n            ascend(cx, cy, z, cyaw)\n            continue\n\n        ascend(cx, cy, z, cyaw)\n\n        # --- place ---\n        move(bx, by, SAFE_Z, byaw)              # pad yaw == bin yaw, so the cube is square to the bin\n        release_z = CUBE + 0.020                # cube bottom ~20 mm above the table, well below the rim\n        descend(bx, by, SAFE_Z, release_z, byaw)\n        suction(False)\n        ascend(bx, by, release_z, byaw)\n\n        calls[0] += 1\n        if api.done():\n            return\n    return\n```\n\nThe policy re-reads the cube and bin poses at run time, picks at the measured pose by creeping down in 1 mm steps until suction confirms a grip, then carries the cube at a safe height and lowers it into the bin of its own colour square to the walls. It checks `done()` and retries up to four times within the call budget.\n\nThe supplied cube reading (y \u2248 -0.30 m, yaw 16.4\u00b0) is outside the stated placement range (y = -0.05 \u00b1 0.05 m, yaw \u00b1 15\u00b0), so I trusted the camera rather than the nominal position. Nothing here was run, and if that reading is a camera error the pick will fail.",
